• {"summary":"No concrete introduced defect found. I read the diff, `scripts/check-verification-integrity.py` and the test additions. I did not run the tests. Both earlier findings are fixed in 0d0c686b. (1) Decorator scope: `python_shadowed_calls` now visits each decorator with the enclosing `scopes` before adding the function's own bindings. It skips the decorators when it walks the children, so `@skip def test(self, skip)` is still flagged (`scripts/check-verification-integrity.py:563`). (2) Comprehension leakage: `collect` now handles a comprehension at the top of the function, so a comprehension nested in `elt`, `iter` or `ifs` is scoped too. Its targets no longer enter `names`, and walrus targets still bind in the enclosing function (`scripts/check-verification-integrity.py:524`). The three deduplications in 9ba18c80 do not change behavior. In `append_literal`, `i` is read at call time and equals the literal's start offset, so `literal_spans[i]` is the same as before. The Call decorator and its `.func` are shadowed together because both compute the same head from the same scopes, so dropping `id(target) in shadowed_calls` changes nothing. `identity_only_suffix` is the same predicate that both call sites inlined."}

